==Battleground==
*20 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1 second<sup>20f~30f</sup>.
*2 [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 100~133.33 seconds<sup>3,000f~4,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The stage begins with a wave of 20 Squire Rels attempting to rush the player. Use [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cats]] and [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to stall them and slowly build up money from killing them, or wipe them all out at once using [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] if necessary. When you reach the enemy base, you should have enough money to upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to level 7 or 8. Deploy a [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] and any long-ranged cat. At this point, Pigge and B.B.Bunny have already come out, so send out a [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave Cat]] and/or [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] in order to slowly stall and kill them.

Teacher Bear should now be on the field. Send out more meatshields and Titans and try to get to the enemy base. When Teacher Bear is killed, destroy the enemy base as soon as possible before another Teacher Bear and a Mooth attempt to destroy your frontline.

An alternative strategy is to rush the level with [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cats]]; make sure to get all superior treasures before Alaska for this strategy to work the best.

